# 'Play game' in the view (R3 of the M10-M14 review; ADR-113): the Viewport
# panel takes the focus when Play game starts, and while it has it the
# game's InputService gets the keys (SDL events the script pushes, never OS
# input). The session's replay records their four edges (run_editor.py
# --expect-edges 4). With the focus on another panel the game gets no key
# down; the release still reaches it and changes nothing.
wait-frames 30
expect-viewport yes
play-game
wait-frames 10
expect-state playing
expect-game-keyboard yes
push-key d
wait-ticks 30
push-key space
wait-frames 2
push-key space up
wait-ticks 30
push-key d up
wait-ticks 30
show-panel Inspector
wait-frames 5
expect-game-keyboard no
push-key d
wait-ticks 20
push-key d up
wait-ticks 10
stop
wait-frames 2
expect-state edit
expect-hash document initial
quit discard
